※ pl4g-test: compile=ok opt=0,1 run=native,qemu exit=92 host=host.c
※ pl4g-test: args -shared

※ What the host defines is known only once there is a host, so a symbol it
※ does not define is found out at the first call, which stops the program with
※ a status of its own (92) and a message saying which symbol it was.

@[host("pl4g_nowhere_to_be_found")]
fn nowhere() → i32

@[visible, cdecl, impure]
fn run() → i32:
    nowhere()
